I've updated my shp credit patch and added a feature that let's the 
player boy the credit back. Jukka Lahtinen has been helpfull by giving a 
site that hosts my patches. It can be find at this URL:

http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html#credit

Description:

The patch affects how credit is purchased from a shopkeeper. Gold 
dropped in a shop does not increase your credit anymore, but on the 
other hand all gold you find in shop is yours to take for free.

If you want to buy credit from a shopkeeper try to (p)ay when you don't 
owe anything. This asks if you want to buy credit and if you answer yes 
you can state the amount you want to buy. The money goes into the 
shopkeepers inventory.

If you have credit and you try to (p)ay without owing anything you are 
asked if you want to withdraw your credit. If you answer yes then the 
shopkeeper tries to pay your credit back. If he has insufficient funds 
then he pays whatever he has. If you don't want to withdraw your credit 
then you are asked if you want to buy more credit.

Sorry, no interest is payed for the capital.

